---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro'
---

<Base
  lang="en"
  title="ROI calculator: what missed calls cost you | Klantkraan"
  description="Work out in 10 seconds how much revenue you lose to missed calls, and how quickly Klantkraan pays for itself."
  centered={false}
>
  <!-- 1. Hero (cream) -->
  <section class="py-10 md:py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6">
      <h1 class="font-display text-hero text-(--color-chalk)">What does a <span class="text-(--color-sodium)">missed call</span> cost you?</h1>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-h3 text-(--color-dim)">
        Enter your numbers. The calculator shows straight away how many jobs you lose in a year and
        how quickly each Klantkraan plan pays for itself.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2. Form + results (stone-100) -->
  <section class="border-y border-(--color-line) bg-[rgba(0,0,0,0.14)] py-10 md:py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-5xl gap-6 md:gap-8 px-6 md:grid-cols-2">
      <form
        id="roi-form"
        class="rounded-(--radius-card) border border-(--color-line) bg-(--color-panel) p-5 md:p-6"
        onsubmit="return false"
      >
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div>
            <label for="calls" class="block text-body font-medium text-(--color-chalk)">
              How many calls do you get per week?
            </label>
            <input
              id="calls"
              name="calls"
              type="number"
              inputmode="numeric"
              autocomplete="off"
              min="0"
              step="1"
              value="40"
              class="mt-2 w-full rounded-(--radius-button) border border-(--color-line) bg-[rgba(0,0,0,0.25)] px-3 py-3 text-body text-(--color-chalk)"
            />
          </div>
          <div>
            <label for="missed" class="block text-body font-medium text-(--color-chalk)">
              % of calls you miss today
            </label>
            <input
              id="missed"
              name="missed"
              type="number"
              inputmode="numeric"
              autocomplete="off"
              min="0"
              max="100"
              step="1"
              value="28"
              class="mt-2 w-full rounded-(--radius-button) border border-(--color-line) bg-[rgba(0,0,0,0.25)] px-3 py-3 text-body text-(--color-chalk)"
            />
            <p class="mt-1 text-small text-(--color-dim)">
              Industry estimate: 28% for installation and roofing trades.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <label for="value" class="block text-body font-medium text-(--color-chalk)">
              Average customer value per job (€)
            </label>
            <input
              id="value"
              name="value"
              type="number"
              inputmode="numeric"
              autocomplete="off"
              min="0"
              step="10"
              value="450"
              class="mt-2 w-full rounded-(--radius-button) border border-(--color-line) bg-[rgba(0,0,0,0.25)] px-3 py-3 text-body text-(--color-chalk)"
            />
            <p class="mt-1 text-small text-(--color-dim)">
              Default €450, the average plumbing job.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </form>

      <aside
        class="rounded-(--radius-card) border border-(--color-sodium) bg-(--color-panel) p-5 md:p-6"
      >
        <h2 class="font-display text-h2 text-(--color-chalk)">Your loss in numbers</h2>
        <div class="mt-4 space-y-4">
          <div>
            <p class="text-small text-(--color-dim)">Missed calls per year</p>
            <p
              id="out-missed-year"
              class="font-display text-h1 tabular-nums [overflow-wrap:anywhere] text-(--color-sodium)"
            >
              0
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="text-small text-(--color-dim)">Lost revenue per year</p>
            <p id="out-lost-revenue" class="font-display text-h1 tabular-nums [overflow-wrap:anywhere] text-(--color-sodium)">
              €0
            </p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-small text-(--color-dim)">
              Assumption: roughly 1 in 3 missed calls would have become a paying job.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <hr class="my-6 border-(--color-line)" />

        <h3 class="font-display text-h3 text-(--color-chalk)">Klantkraan payback time</h3>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-body text-(--color-dim)">
          <li>
            Chat (€299/mo): <span id="out-payback-chat" class="font-mono">–</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            Compleet (€499/mo): <span id="out-payback-compleet" class="font-mono">–</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4 text-small text-(--color-dim)">
          "Payback time" = the number of months until the plan is paid for by the revenue you win back.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3. How we calculate (cream) -->
  <section class="py-10 md:py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6">
      <p class="eyebrow">Method</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-h2 text-(--color-chalk)">How we calculate</h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-body text-(--color-dim)">
        <li>Missed calls per year = calls per week × 52 × (% missed / 100).</li>
        <li>
          Lost revenue per year = missed calls × customer value × 33% conversion. So we only count
          1 in 3 missed calls as a lost job; without a callback system, most callers give up.
        </li>
        <li>
          Payback time = plan price ÷ (lost revenue per year ÷ 12). The bigger your pile of missed
          jobs, the faster Klantkraan pays for itself.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <a
        href="/en/demo/"
        class="mt-8 btn btn-primary btn-lg"
      >
        Have us check it live on your numbers
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 4. Werkspot math (stone-100) -->
  <section class="border-y border-(--color-line) bg-[rgba(0,0,0,0.14)] py-10 md:py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6">
      <p class="eyebrow">Lead platforms</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-h2 text-(--color-chalk)">And what does a job through Werkspot cost?</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-body text-(--color-dim)">
        On lead platforms you pay per lead, and the same lead also goes to your competitors.
        Whoever responds first wins the job; the rest paid too. Compare that with a fixed price
        for your own channel, where every caller simply gets answered.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="rounded-(--radius-card) border border-(--color-line) bg-(--color-panel) p-5">
          <p class="font-display text-h1 tabular-nums text-(--color-sodium)">€3&ndash;75</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-small text-(--color-dim)">
            for a single lead on Werkspot, even when the job goes to someone else.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-(--radius-card) border border-(--color-line) bg-(--color-panel) p-5">
          <p class="font-display text-h1 tabular-nums text-(--color-sodium)">&plusmn;€208</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-small text-(--color-dim)">
            in lead fees per job actually won, as calculated by
            <a href="https://adaptoo.nl/blog/werkspot-kosten" class="underline">Adaptoo</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-(--radius-card) border border-(--color-sodium) bg-(--color-panel) p-5">
          <p class="font-display text-h1 tabular-nums text-(--color-chalk)">€0 per lead</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-small text-(--color-dim)">
            through your own number and website. Klantkraan is a fixed monthly price, however
            many jobs you take on.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-body text-(--color-dim)">
        Your own channel also grows in value: every review, every returning customer and every
        referral belongs to you, not to the platform.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 5. E-mail course opt-in (cream). The calculator above stays e-mail-free: this form is
       a separate, optional offer. Native POST works without JS (the API 303s back with
       ?cursus=ok|fout); rekentool.js upgrades it to fetch() + inline result. -->
  <section class="py-10 md:py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-5xl gap-6 md:gap-8 px-6 md:grid-cols-[1fr_.9fr] md:items-start">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Free e-mail course</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-h2 text-(--color-chalk)">
          Tackle your missed revenue in 4 lessons
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-body text-(--color-dim)">
          Four short e-mails over nine days, written for tradespeople with a full schedule.
          Practical, no sales pitch, and everything can be applied yourself. The lessons are
          in Dutch.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-body text-(--color-dim)">
          <li>Lesson 1: the job that went to someone else.</li>
          <li>Lesson 2: what a lead costs when you buy it back.</li>
          <li>Lesson 3: three things you can fix yourself this week.</li>
          <li>Lesson 4: if you want to automate it.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4 text-small text-(--color-dim)">Unsubscribe with one click under any lesson.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <!-- method+action are the zero-JS fallback: the browser posts the form itself and
             the API answers with a 303 back to this page with ?cursus=ok|fout. -->
        <form
          id="cursus-form"
          method="POST"
          action="https://demo.klantkraan.nl/api/cursus"
          data-astro-reload
          class="rounded-(--radius-card) border border-(--color-line) bg-(--color-panel) p-5 md:p-6"
        >
          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div>
              <label for="cursus-naam" class="block text-body font-medium text-(--color-chalk)">
                First name <span class="font-normal text-(--color-dim)">(optional)</span>
              </label>
              <input
                id="cursus-naam"
                name="naam"
                type="text"
                autocomplete="given-name"
                class="mt-2 w-full rounded-(--radius-button) border border-(--color-line) bg-[rgba(0,0,0,0.25)] px-3 py-3 text-body text-(--color-chalk)"
              />
            </div>
            <div>
              <label for="cursus-email" class="block text-body font-medium text-(--color-chalk)">
                E-mail
              </label>
              <input
                id="cursus-email"
                name="email"
                type="email"
                required
                autocomplete="email"
                class="mt-2 w-full rounded-(--radius-button) border border-(--color-line) bg-[rgba(0,0,0,0.25)] px-3 py-3 text-body text-(--color-chalk)"
              />
            </div>
            <div class="hp" aria-hidden="true">
              <label for="cursus-website">Website</label>
              <input id="cursus-website" name="website" type="text" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" />
            </div>
            <p id="cursus-error" class="hidden text-small text-(--color-sodium)" role="alert">
              Something went wrong. Check your e-mail address and try again.
            </p>
            <button type="submit" id="cursus-submit" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg w-full justify-center">
              Send me lesson 1
            </button>
            <p class="text-small text-(--color-dim)">
              Lesson 1 lands in your inbox right away. No newsletter, no spam.
            </p>
          </div>
        </form>
        <div
          id="cursus-success"
          class="hidden rounded-(--radius-card) border border-(--color-sodium) bg-(--color-panel) p-5 md:p-6"
        >
          <h3 class="font-display text-h3 text-(--color-chalk)">Lesson 1 is on its way</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-body text-(--color-dim)">
            Check your inbox, and your spam folder just in case. The next lessons follow
            automatically.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Externalised JS (loaded as same-origin to pass strict CSP script-src 'self'). -->
  <script src="/js/rekentool.js" type="module" is:inline></script>
</Base>

<style>
  /* Honeypot: parked off-screen so humans never see it; bots that fill it are dropped. */
  .hp {
    position: absolute;
    left: -9999px;
    top: auto;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
</style>
